-- WotLK raids: restore the 25-man normal spawns that were lost when the 4.3.4 spawnMask was converted to SkyFire's
-- one-bit-per-DifficultyID masks (every spawn on these maps was set to 8, 10N only).
-- MapDifficulty.dbc (5.4.8) has DifficultyID 3 (10N) and 4 (25N) for all seven maps, and also 5 (10H) and 6 (25H)
-- for Icecrown Citadel and Trial of the Crusader. Reference mask bits 0, 1, 2, 3 (10N, 25N, 10H, 25H) become 8, 16, 32, 64.
-- Heroic bits are NOT set: SkyFire's 4-argument RAID_MODE is (10N, 25N, flex, lfr), so the 41 TC style
-- RAID_MODE(10N, 25N, 10H, 25H) calls in the Icecrown Citadel and Trial of the Crusader scripts return the 25N value in
-- heroic modes. Spawns whose reference mask is heroic only are left at 8.
-- Maps where the 4.3.4 mask is the same for the whole map use one map-wide statement; the others use per-guid lists
-- matched by entry and position (within 1 yard) to the 4.3.4 spawn (3.3.5 as fallback). Every statement is guarded by
-- map and spawnMask = 8, so the file is safe to run twice. Unmatched spawns keep 8.

